    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1947-01-30">January 30, 1947</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                        >Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__394" type="person">Gerhard Colm</rs> sent me your
                    letter of January 15,<note type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.
                        <!-- vermutlich Brief L11036 --></note> in which you inquire about the
                    possibility of visiting <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place"
                        >Germany</rs>. Unfortunately, I was out of town for a few days and did not
                    get to answering your letter earlier.</p>
                <p>I am aware of the correspondence between <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1390"
                        type="person">Reinhold Niebuhr</rs> and <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4911"
                        type="person">Eugene Anderson</rs> in my Division, and know that <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__4911" type="person">Mr. Anderson</rs> has referred
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1390" type="person">Niebuhr</rs>&apos;s letter
                    to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4912" type="person">Lieutenant Colonel R. B.
                        McRae</rs> of the Reorientation Branch, Civil Affairs Division, War
                    Department, with a personal recommendation that your case be favorably
                    considered. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4912" type="person">Lt. Col. McRae</rs>
                    is the Chief of the Reorientation Branch.</p>
                <p>As <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4911" type="person">Anderson</rs> wrote to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1390" type="person">Niebuhr</rs>, the
                    administrative arrangements for official trips to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> by experts in the
                    field of education and information are made by the Reorientation Branch. This
                    also answers one of your questions in your letter to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__394" type="person">Colm</rs>. The only
                    appropriations available for American experts to be sent to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> for contributing to
                    German reorientation appear on the War Department budget.</p>
                <p>These so-called experts are requested by Military Government either by name or by
                    indication of their qualifications, to be put on the War Department payrole for
                    a limited period of time in order to assist Military Government in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> in an educational or
                    informational task which is considered important.</p>
                <p>Neither the War Department nor the Department of State has at present any funds
                    for financing any other visits of American to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122"
                        type="place">Germany</rs>.</p>
                <p>As to the possibility of an arra<supplied>n</supplied>gement as envisaged by <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__4913" type="person">Professor Douglas
                    Steer</rs>,<!-- Identität nicht ganz sicher, würde aber in den Zusammenhang passen. -->
                    mentioned in your letter to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__394" type="person"
                        >Colm</rs>, I should be inclined to think that the <add place="sublinear"
                        >best</add> procedure would be for<note type="ea">Darunter findet sich die
                        Adresse <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                        >Tillichs</rs>.</note><pb n="2"/>
                    <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4913" type="person">Professor Steer</rs> or the
                    Society of Friends to approach the Reorientation Branch of the State Department
                    as sprecifically as possible with precisely what they have in mind.</p>
                <p>If you have any further questions regarding your plans, do not hesitate to call
                    me.</p>


                <closer>
                    <salute> Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1823" type="person">Hans Speier</rs>,<lb/>
                        Associate Chief, Division of Occupied Areas<lb/> Office of International
                        Information<lb/> and Cultural Affairs</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>cc: <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__394" type="person">Mr. Gerhard Colm</rs>,
                        Council of Economic Advisers, Washington, 25 <del rend="s">attachments</del>
                        with the letter adressed to him by <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
